<!-- RUT_Ported_ResearchTrio.xml - RESEARCH_TRIO_RETIRE_1 (owner card 2026-09-18,
     "port all 17, then cut" - supersedes an earlier same-day "port the 4 ruled"
     card). These 18 ResearchProjectDefs are the ONLY place these defNames now
     exist, replacing petetimessix.researchreinvented.steppingstones (10 rows)
     and als.gravtech + als.gravtech.bc (7 + 1 = 8 rows: 7 named by the escalation
     plus GravEngineBuild, a genuine gap in both the original escalation's
     17-defName table and research_manifest_draft.csv - it has no manifest row
     at all, yet is a real als.gravtech ResearchProjectDef and a live prereq of
     both AdvShipParts and GravForge below. Left unported it would have silently
     broken the same prereq chain this whole item exists to protect, so it is
     ported here as an 18th row on the same reasoning as its siblings).

     SAME DEFNAMES ON PURPOSE - the Absorbed_KotorCore/Absorbed_AdditionalMods
     precedent (WEAPONS_DONOR_RETIREMENT_1): every external cross-reference
     (our own RUT_ResearchRetag.xml / RUT_ResearchTabAssign.xml, any other
     active mod's researchPrerequisites) keeps resolving with ZERO repointing,
     because RimPatch applies against the merged Defs database regardless of
     which mod authored the base def. This IS the PORT TRAP the owner's ruling
     named: these files must stay held (DEPLOY_HOLD.txt) until the three donor
     packageIds are OUT of ModsConfig.xml, then deployed in the same change -
     deploying same-defName content while the donor is still active produces a
     silent duplicate-defName collision (RimWorld keeps only the first loaded).

     VALUES: cost/tab per infrastructure/output/research_manifest_draft.csv
     (2026-09-04, RESEARCH_RECOST_PREREQ_JOIN_1) wherever the manifest's number
     is what src/RimUtinni/ResearchRetag/Patches/RUT_ResearchRetag.xml and
     RUT_ResearchTabAssign.xml ACTUALLY apply live today (verified line-by-line
     against both patch files before writing this file) - baseCost 5200 flat
     for the 8-row GravTech/BigCannons cluster, tab per RUT_ResearchTabAssign's
     existing per-defName entries. Everything else (techLevel, requiredResearch
     Building/Facilities, tags, techprint/heldByFactionCategoryTags, generalRules,
     discoveredLetter text) copied from the donors' own shipped XML (workshop
     2868389782 v1.6/Defs/ResearchProjectDefs_{Basic,Electricity}.xml;
     workshop 3545374124 1.6/Defs/Research_GT.xml; workshop 3628174105
     1.6/Defs/Research_GTbc.xml), read directly off disk this session, never
     from memory.

     PREREQS: two rows (AdvShipParts, GravBionics) have a manifest-recommended
     prereq that DIFFERS from what is actually live - checked, no patch in this
     repo or in vanillaexpanded.gravship (the only other mod with any plausible
     reason to touch them) applies the manifest's proposal. Ported here with the
     LIVE prereqs (AdvShipParts: ShipComputerCore+GravEngineBuild, donor raw;
     GravBionics: GravTuning+Bionics, donor raw) rather than the manifest's
     unapplied GravTuning-only / GravForge-only recommendation, so this port is
     a pure retirement (zero tree-shape change) and does not silently execute a
     reshaping decision nobody has actually ruled on. Re-tabling those two
     rows' prereqs, if wanted, is a separate call for the owner.

     The 5 Jawa Scavenging rows (RR_BasicApparel/BasicCraftingFacilities/
     BasicFoodPrep/IncendiaryWeapons) carry VFET_* prereqs, not steppingstones'
     own RR_Organization/RR_Fire/RR_BasicFurniture/RR_BasicRangedWeapons - that
     remap is fully live today via the donor's OWN submod-compat patch
     (ModSpecific/v1.6/VFE_Tribals/Patches/Patches_ResearchProjectDefs_RR_to_VFET.xml,
     a custom RR.PatchOperationResearchPrereg class inside the donor's own
     assembly, firing because OskarPotocki.VFE.Tribals is active). That patch
     dies with the donor, so its resolved output is baked directly into these
     native defs instead of re-implemented as a patch - equivalent end state,
     no assembly dependency.

     RR_ElectricityBasics ships with NO prerequisites element, on purpose - the
     QUICKTEST_POSTSETUP_CRASH_1 self-loop
     (src/RimMandrake/MandrakePatches/Patches/RRElectricityBasicsSelfPrereq_Fix.xml)
     can only exist if this def carries a prerequisites list a later patch can
     corrupt; omitting it here removes the bug at the source, and per this
     item's own execution spec that now-redundant fix file is deleted in the
     same change (nothing MayRequires the donor's packageId now that the donor
     is gone; it would only ever have been a no-op FindMod).

     GravWeapon and GravBionics: owner rulings 2026-09-01/09-04 name both as
     Rust Cathedral boon-gated (RustCathedralDroids), NOT plain purchasable
     techprints - but the actual gating MECHANISM (bespoke grant vs.
     heldByFactionCategoryTags vs. something else) is explicitly undecided,
     tracked separately as TECHPRINT_FACTION_GATING_1. Both rows are ported
     here MECHANICALLY IDENTICAL to their current live state (ungated, no
     techprint fields - matching the donor's own shipped XML, which also
     carries none for either row) so this port changes nothing about how they
     unlock today; only a comment flags the deferred ruling for whoever builds
     TECHPRINT_FACTION_GATING_1.
-->
